hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23885","Isma'il narrated to us, Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us from Abu Nadrah, one who heard the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle of the days of Tashriq narrated to me, and said: O people, your Lord is one and your father is one, there is no merit of an Arab over a non-Arab, nor of a non-Arab over an Arab, nor of a red over a black, nor a black over a red, except by piety, have I conveyed, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has conveyed, then he said: What day is this, they said: A sacred day, then he said: What month is this, they said: A sacred month, he said: Then he said: What land is this, they said: A sacred land, he said: Allah has made sacred among you your blood and your wealth, he said, and I do not know whether he said: or your honors or not, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, have I conveyed, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has conveyed, he said: Let the witness convey to the absent."
